# Native acceleration shims

The vectorizer and rasterizer can hand off to a native backend when a shim
is present next to this file. Discovery order: C++ -> C# -> Java.

## C++ (fastest)

    cl /LD /O2 /EHsc logo_vec.cpp /Fe:liblogo_vec.dll

Exposes `int logo_vec_trace(const uint8_t* rgba, int w, int h, char* out_svg, int cap)`.

## C# (Windows-only, pythonnet)

    csc /target:library /out:LogoVec.dll logo_vec.cs

Loaded via `clr.AddReference("LogoVec")`.

## Java (cross-platform, py4j)

    javac -d build LogoVec.java
    java -cp build logo.LogoVec --port 25334 &

Point `py4j` at the gateway port. Slower JNI hop than the C++ path.

If none are present, the host falls back to `pure_python` and logs a notice.